  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1256 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nPresent model agreement does continues to see the expected trough\npush across the Panhandles early Thursday morning with its full\nexit following later that evening. Showers are possible alongside\nthis trough with present ensembles giving us around a 20 to 40\npercent chance of rain showers in the Northeastern Panhandles.\nMoving into Friday, most models do see another ridge building in\nacross the Southwestern United States, which will lead to\nnorthwesterly upper-level flow across the Panhandles. While this\nshould leave us rather dry for Friday, there have been hints in\nthe GFS and ECMWF of a short-wave trough pushing across this flow\nlater this weekend. However, present agreement between the\nensembles has not seen much potential out this wave, with current\ntrends now dropping our chance of precipitation below 10 percent\nthrough the entire weekend. Regardless, temperature will stay cool\nunder this flow with afternoon highs holding in the low to mid\n60s. Meanwhile, overnight and morning lows will start get more of\nthat late fall feel with locations seeing temperatures in the 30s.",
